  "out_of_scope_edits": [],
  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. The premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel`, and removing it would break that service.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34`** parses `OrderPlaced` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. A missing `channel` makes it reject the whole event with a `ContractViolationError`. Its test at `test/ingest.test.ts:88` (\"requires channel\") asserts exactly that.\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17`** copies `channel` into the `orders` table row. The table has a `channel` column, and `README.md:23-31` documents it as part of the contract.\n- **`billing-service`** only has `channel` in its test helpers. `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106` passes `channel: undefined`, so billing doesn't appear to need it.\n\nIf I dropped `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event in `orders-service`, analytics ingestion would reject every new order event.\n\nDropping it from the order model and the event touches these places in `orders-service`:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: the `CHANNELS` constant, the `Channel` type, both interfaces, and the validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`\n- The tests and helpers.\n- The `createApp` example in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n\nIt would also change the API: `POST /orders` would no longer require `channel`.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. Remove `channel` from `orders-service` anyway, if analytics-ingest is being changed separately. That repo is read-only for me, so its team would need to make the change first or at the same time.\n2. Remove it from the order model and API but keep it in the event, which would need a source for the value. That doesn't match what you asked for.\n3. Hold off until the analytics team confirms they can drop the field.\n\nI'd go with option 3 or a coordinated rollout. Tell me which one and I'll make the changes.",
